            <div xml:id="d909">

                <pb facs="0938" n="826" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg826"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 853.00/95.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Portuguese Minister to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Portuguese Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-10-07"><hi rendition="#italic">October 7,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Most Illustrious and Excellent Sir</hi>: By the way
                    of information I have the honor to advise your excellency that I have received
                    from Lisbon a telegram reading as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Portuguese Legation, New
                                York</hi>.</p>
                        <p>Lisbon, October 6–10.—Republic proclaimed. Provisional Government
                            presided over by Dr. Theophilo Braza. Please communicate happy
                            intelligence to Government and our fellow countrymen. Perfect order. <hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Bernardino Machado</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Minister of Foreign Affairs.</hi></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I avail, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Viscount de Alte.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
